# E-commerce Transition Complete! 🎉

I have successfully transformed LoomistryStudio from a single-page landing site into a fully functional, multi-page e-commerce store. 

All phases of the implementation plan have been completed. 

## What changed?

### 1. Global Navigation & Routing
Your website now uses `react-router-dom` to provide instant, seamless navigation between different pages without ever reloading the browser. 

### 2. Global State Management (Zustand)
I implemented a robust shopping cart state using `zustand`. It handles:
- Adding items (and automatically grouping identical items)
- Updating quantities
- Removing items
- Calculating the real-time subtotal
- Persisting the cart's open/closed state across all pages

### 3. New Pages Built
- **Home (`/`)**: Your original landing page layout, perfectly preserved.
- **Shop (`/shop`)**: A beautiful, grid-based catalog showing all available handcrafted rugs.
- **Product Details (`/product/:id`)**: A dedicated page for each rug showing a large image, detailed description, size selector, and an "Add to Cart" button.
- **Checkout (`/checkout`)**: A fully styled, responsive checkout flow that captures user details, displays an order summary, and simulates order processing.

### 4. Cart Drawer
Added a sleek, slide-out cart drawer that appears when you add a product or click the cart icon in the navigation bar. You can manage your items directly within the drawer before proceeding to checkout.

## How to Test

Since your Vite development server (`npm run dev`) is still running in the background, your website has already updated automatically!

1. Open your browser to `http://localhost:5173/`
2. Scroll down to the **"Our Rug Collection"** section and click "View Details" on any rug.
3. On the **Product Page**, select a size and click **"Add to Cart"**.
4. The **Cart Drawer** will automatically slide open.
5. Try increasing the quantity or removing an item.
6. Click **"Checkout Now"** to view the checkout page.
7. Fill in some dummy details and click **"Place Order"** to see the success screen!

## Next Steps

> [!NOTE]  
> Currently, the checkout uses a simulated delay. When you are ready to take real payments, we can integrate a payment provider like **Stripe** or **Razorpay**. We can also connect a database (like Supabase) to permanently store the product data instead of hardcoding it.

Let me know what you'd like to work on next!
